<title>SWEDEN: Swedish March unemployment falls to 8.4 percent.</title>
<headline>Swedish March unemployment falls to 8.4 percent.</headline>
<dateline>STOCKHOLM 1997-04-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Unemployment in Sweden fell to 8.4 percent in March from 8.8 percent in February, Statistics Sweden said on Friday.</p>
<p> SWEDISH UNEMPLOYMENT	 March '97   March '96  Feb '97</p>
<p> Percent of workforce	 8.4	   7.4	  8.8</p>
<p> Number of unemployed	 355,000     314,000    372,000</p>
<p>Note - A Reuters poll of economists showed the market had expected an unemployment rate of 8.4 percent in March. Sweden's labour market board (Ams) released its March unemployment figures last week, showing unemployment of 8.0 percent.</p>
<p>-- Stockholm newsroom +46-8-700-1017</p>
</text>
